# Ignore file for the E2E frontend image (e2e/docker/frontend.e2e.Dockerfile).
#
# BuildKit uses "<Dockerfile name>.dockerignore" from the Dockerfile's own directory in preference
# to a .dockerignore at the root of the build context:
#   docker buildx build -f e2e/docker/frontend.e2e.Dockerfile frontend
#
# Part 1 is a verbatim copy of frontend/.dockerignore (scripts/preflight.sh checks every line of
# it is still present). Part 2 keeps local env files (.env.local, .env.production.local, ...) out
# of the build: `next build` would otherwise inline their NEXT_PUBLIC_* values into the bundle and
# override the build-arg that points the UI at the E2E backend (http://127.0.0.1:43080).

# --- part 1: identical to frontend/.dockerignore ------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.next/
Notes.md
README.md
# Secrets and local env files never enter the image. `next build` would also inline NEXT_PUBLIC_* values from
# .env* files into the bundle and override the --build-arg NEXT_PUBLIC_BACKEND_URL.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
**/*.pem
# Local tool state and caches
.git
.claude-flow/
*.rvf
*.rvf.lock

# --- part 2: E2E additions ----------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
.git
.claude-flow/
